<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Canton of Schwyz</h1><p class="st-meta">1240 CE – 1798 CE · capital Schwyz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Alpine valley community that gave Switzerland its name and flag, a founding member of the Confederacy and victor over the Habsburgs at Morgarten.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The free peasants of Schwyz, at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mythen">Mythen</a>, gained a charter of imperial immediacy from Frederick II at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-faenza">Faenza</a> in 1240. In 1291 they joined Uri and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-unterwalden">Unterwalden</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-charter-of-1291">Federal Charter</a>, and in 1315 they defeated a <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-morgarten">Morgarten</a>, securing their independence and lending their name to the whole <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/old-swiss-confederacy">Swiss Confederacy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landsgemeinde">Landsgemeinde</a> of all free men elected the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landammann">Landammann</a>, and leading families dominated politics. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">Cattle</a>, transit trade and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> service supported the canton. Schwyz quarrelled with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/einsiedeln-abbey">Einsiedeln Abbey</a> over pasture, expanded into the March and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hofe-district">Höfe</a>, and fought <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/canton-of-zurich">Zürich</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-zurich-war">Old Zürich War</a>. It stayed firmly Catholic and led the Catholic cantons after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1798 Schwyz resisted the French under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alois-von-reding">Alois von Reding</a> but was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a>. It was restored as a canton in 1803 and remains one today; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-charter-of-1291">Federal Charter</a> is kept in its archive.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1240 CE – 1798 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.38%;width:11.10%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1240 CE – 1798 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Schwyz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alois von Reding</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alemannic German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Schwyz</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1519&amp;focus=canton-of-schwyz" aria-label="Canton of Schwyz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4883 527 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Canton of Schwyz lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5203 783L5186 782M5203 783L5188 772"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5186 782h0M5188 772h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5203 783h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5203 783h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Schwyz. <a href="/atlas?year=1519&amp;focus=canton-of-schwyz">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
